# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
#
# RDR-BAR: the reader's own command bar, and the highlight it hands back
# (#329, #330) - open the log, open a page, come back to the log, and
# leave, with the screen the journal was opened over coming back whole.
# Two defects a person found on a display. Every bar this game draws
# starts at column zero with one space between its commands, where the
# reader's read ` NEXT   PREV   EXIT` (#329); and every bar this game
# draws paints the initial white and the tail green, where the reader's
# was one call in the bright (#330).
# A single leg, for not-log-giveback.leg's reason: `N` reaches the
# program in a seam-off run. Since #330 the `Notes` splice hands the
# program's own bar highlight byte (`0x6B2B`, M5-E1g #304) back on the
# way out, so the give-back is exact on the bar row too.
# Driven by hand on the shorter boot (`--code-wheel-answered`, #291).

about the reader's own bar, and the highlight the Notes splice hands back
kind single
program START.EXE
store tests/visual/reader-store.txt
cite-all
both code-wheel

# The boot #291 left. The runner carries the flag as of this change and this
# is the first leg to ask for it; #293 owes every leg before it the same
# re-drive.
code-wheel-answered

# No `document` line, and that is #290 rather than an omission: no seam in
# this build is gated now. camp-fix-exit.leg is the same shape.
seam journal
until 300000000
every 25

# Slot A, the log, a page of the entry the log's cursor is on, back to the
# log by the bar's own `EXIT`, and out by it again. A screen this seam
# draws is painted over successive arrivals and is slow to appear - about
# 230 frames for a twenty-row page (#305) - so every range below starts
# well clear of the key that opened it.
key L@7550
key A@7800
key N@9600
key Return@10800
key E@12000
key E@13200

# Each screen, holding still with nothing pressed. Measured: the listing is
# one hash from 9,725 to 10,800, the page one from 11,050 to 12,000, and
# the listing again one from 12,100 to 13,200.
same 9800-10775
same 11100-11975
same 12200-13175

# The listing a page was opened from is the listing it comes back to,
# whole: the two ranges above are the same hash, not merely each steady.
equal 9800 12200

# And the screen the journal was opened over, back again after it - every
# pixel, with nothing excepted, byte for byte from 13,425 to the end of the
# run (15,086 frames). Driven once more with the give-back taken out and
# nothing else changed, this line reports `frame 13500 is not frame 9575
# again: 190 pixels differ, box 9,192,311,198` - the bar row and nothing
# but it. The `same` ranges hold either way, a highlight that never moves
# being a screen that holds perfectly still.
equal 9575 13500
